tal_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.5.1.stable and 4.6.beta2\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable.mono unknown - CachyOS Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri, 19 Dec 2025 01:23:45 +0000 on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2070 (nvidia; 590.48.01) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800X3D 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.26 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using the color picker with the editor Prefer Wayland option enabled, should the user hold down click on any element, and then move outside the color picker window and let go, moving the mouse back into the color picker will cause it to continue manipulating whatever element. \nThis issue does not occur on XWayland.\n\n\n(It's rather hard to demonstrate in this clip, but assume I let go of the mouse when I leave the color picker window)\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d29f6e65-fe15-4970-ac05-42d6a1380c6e\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nEnable the Prefer Wayland option in the editor\nCause a color picker to open, ColorRect was the simplest for me in this case.\nHold down left click on any of the elements, as if you were to normally use the color picker.\nMove the mouse outside of the window, then let go of left click\nMoving the mouse back into the color picker should cause the color picker to still believe left click is held. \n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}